        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm working through the root अक्ष् (to pervade/reach), bhvādi parasmaipadī, with its iṭ/veṭ augment status, trying to derive the future tense middle-person plural form by working through the sandhi of अक्ष् + स्य.\n\nTracing the संयोगादि लोप rule: since अक्ष् contains the conjunct क्ष् (क्+ष्) before the स् of स्य, the initial क् of the conjunct gets elided, giving अष्, then षढोः कः सि converts it back to अक्, yielding अक्ष्य → अक्ष्यति for third person, so the form I want is अक्ष्यथ, though अक्षिष्यथ with the iṭ augment also works and is the one I'll settle on.\n\n",
